sentences.text:
The present petition has been preferred for following reliefs:
(i) directing the Respondents-authorities to pay the amount of compensation to the petitioner with interest & solatium as per National Highways Act, 1956 (hereinafter referred to as the N.H.Act), Patna High Court CWJC No.8691 of 2022(7)
dt.12-02-2024 as well as under Right to Fair Compensation Transparency in Land Acquisition Rehabilitation & Resettlement Act 30 of 2013 (hereinafter referred to as RFCTLARR Act, 2013), as the residential house of the petitioner has been demolished Ramlal Paswan vs The State Of Bihar on 12 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/184807599/
1 unauthorizedly by the respondents authorities without following the Procedure laid down under the Act;
(ii) directing the Respondents-authorities to restore the possession of the petitioner on the demolished house/area wherefrom the petitioner and his family members have been illegally dispossessed at the hands of the respondents authorities, and also direct the Respondents- authorities to pay the amount of damage etc. to the petitioner for the said illegal dispossession;

(iii) holding and declaring that land/ house in question was not under the public land and the Respondents-authorities were not authorized under any Act to demolish the long standing pucca- residential building of the petitioner especially without issuing notice to the petitioner and without initiating any proceeding under any Act;
(iv) holding and declaring that the lands/property in question is out and out raiyati and khatiyani lands of the petitioner and la Respondents -National Highways are duty bound to pay the amount of compensation to the petitioner under the N.H. Act. 1956 before utilizing the same Patna High Court CWJC No.8691 of 2022(7) dt.12-02-2024 for N.H. road;
(v) restraining the Respondents- authorities, especially the NH authorities from utilizing and/or making proposed constructing on the lands in question, until the adequate amount of compensation and damage is paid to the petitioner.
3. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the matter relates to his raiyati land under Mouja-Simrahi, Thana No.-11, P.S. & Anchal- Basopatti, in the district of Madhubani on which he was residing with his family after constructing his house which was demolished by the respondent-authorities on 28.02.2022 without resorting to any proceeding under Bihar Land Encroachment Act (henceforth for short, 'the Act') .

